Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 07:56:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 069/154] feat(chrome): drift the window tint toward the page
 in front
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The chrome gave no signal about which page was showing. The space tint
stays the base and the page's declared colour is a bounded shift on top,
so a space still reads as itself.

The shift is refused wherever it would cost the chrome's own text its
contrast: the drift walks back toward the space tint until it clears
WCAG AA large. Sampling is driven by a navigation commit and a
theme-color change, so nothing reads the page on a timer.

Off restores the space tint through its own path. ApplyPageTint declines
to touch the window while the setting is off, which is what keeps it free
on every navigation, so it cannot also be what puts the tint back.

ParseHexColor moves out of the controller into atrium_hex_color, shared
by both callers rather than copied.

ATRIUM_CORE_ABI_VERSION 31 -> 32.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
